course: dictionary
lesson: 11110
title: Whirlwind
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A whirlwind is a column of air that spins very fast, like a small tornado. Many words have a science meaning and an everyday meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. «A bagless vacuum spins the air like a whirlwind, flinging dust to the sides of the bin» is about air moving, so it is the science meaning.
explain: Whirlwind can also describe busy, rushed or exciting times. In a sentence like «a whirlwind of activity», the clue is what comes after the word. Ask yourself: is something spinning round in the air, or is a lot happening very fast? The second meaning fits when people, plans or events are moving at great speed.
explain: Look for the common phrases: a whirlwind of, a whirlwind tour, like a whirlwind. Then try the swap test. Put "very fast and busy" in place of whirlwind and check whether the sentence still makes sense. If it does, you have the right meaning.
fact: A whirlwind is a column of air that spins very fast, like a small tornado.
fact: A whirlwind of activity is a lot of things happening very fast.
fact: A whirlwind trip or romance is one that is very quick.
fact: Whirlwind can be a noun (a whirlwind) or used before a noun, as in a whirlwind tour.
fact: Common phrases: a whirlwind of, whirlwind tour, like a whirlwind.
exercise: «A bagless vacuum spins the air like a whirlwind, flinging dust to the sides of the bin.» What is a whirlwind here? | A bag that holds the dust | A loud noise from the kitchen | A tiny bug that buzzes near the bin | *A column of air that spins very fast
exercise: What does «a whirlwind of activity» mean? | A quiet, empty room | A slow walk around the park | *A lot of things happening very fast | A strong wind that blows leaves
exercise: «The old story that scientists proved bumblebees cannot fly came from a rough sum treating a bee wing like a stiff aeroplane wing.» Find and copy one word that means not bendy. | story | sum | rough | *stiff
test: Ella says a whirlwind trip is a trip with lots of spinning air. What does whirlwind trip really mean? | A trip in a windy storm | *A very quick trip | A trip to a dusty bin | A trip where you spin round and round
test: Which sentence uses whirlwind in the science meaning? | «The whirlwind of questions made her dizzy.» | *«Dust flew up in a whirlwind outside the school.» | «We had a whirlwind tour of the museum.» | «His whirlwind romance ended quickly.»
exam: Read «real bee wings flap about 200 times a second and make tiny whirlwinds that give lift.» What are the tiny whirlwinds? | Loud buzzing noises from the wings | Tiny bees that fly in circles | *Small swirls of air made by fast flapping, which help the bee lift | Slow, gentle breezes near the flowers
